      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Terms imported from Other Specifications",
      "pageStart": 5,
      "pageEnd": 7,
      "target": "../sections/sec-013-terms-imported-from-other-specifications.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "In the internal representation a JSON object is described as a map (see [INFRA]), composed of entries with key/value pairs.\nIn the Application Programming Interface, a map is described using a [WEBIDL] record.\nnull\nThe use of the null value within JSON-LD is used to ignore or reset values. A map entry in the @context where the value, or the @id of the value, is\nnull, explicitly decouples a term's association with an IRI. A map entry in the body of a JSON-LD document whose value is null has the same\nmeaning as if the map entry was not defined. If @value, @list, or @set is set to null in expande",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
