    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-014",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "JSON-LD Specific Term Definitions",
      "pageStart": 7,
      "pageEnd": 8,
      "target": "../sections/sec-014-json-ld-specific-term-definitions.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "A JSON-LD Processor is a system which can perform the algorithms defined in JSON-LD 1.1 Processing Algorithms and API. See the Conformance\nsection in JSON-LD 1.1 API for a formal description.\nJSON-LD value\nA JSON-LD value is a string, a number, true or false, a typed value, or a language-tagged string. It represents an RDF literal.\nkeyword\nA string that is specific to JSON-LD, described in the Syntax Tokens and Keywords section of JSON-LD 1.1, and normatively specified in the\nKeywords section of JSON-LD 1.1,\nlanguage map\nAn language map is a map value of a term defined with @container set to @",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-015",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Design Goals and Rationale",
      "pageStart": 8,
      "pageEnd": 9,
      "target": "../sections/sec-015-15-design-goals-and-rationale.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Compatibility\nA JSON-LD document is always a valid JSON document. This ensures that all of the standard JSON libraries work seamlessly with JSON-LD\ndocuments.\nExpressiveness\nThe syntax serializes labeled directed graphs. This ensures that almost every real world data model can be expressed.\nTerseness\nThe JSON-LD syntax is very terse and human readable, requiring as little effort as possible from the developer.\nZero Edits, most of the time\nJSON-LD ensures a smooth and simple transition from existing JSON-based systems. In many cases, zero edits to the JSON document and the\naddition of one line",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-016",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Note",
      "pageStart": 9,
      "pageEnd": 9,
      "target": "../sections/sec-016-note.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Although not discussed in this specification, parallel work using YAML Ain’t Markup Language (YAML™) Version 1.2 [YAML] and binary\nrepresentations such as Concise Binary Object Representation (CBOR) [RFC7049] could be used to map into the internal representation, allowing the\nJSON-LD 1.1 API [JSON-LD11-API] to operate as if the source was a JSON document.\nThis section is non-normative.\nJSON-LD specifies a number of syntax tokens and keywords that are a core part of the language. A normative description of the keywords is given in\n§ 9.16 Keywords.\n:\nThe separator for JSON keys and values that u",
