      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Syntax Tokens and Keywords",
      "pageStart": 9,
      "pageEnd": 10,
      "target": "../sections/sec-018-17-syntax-tokens-and-keywords.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Used to define the short-hand names that are used throughout a JSON-LD document. These short-hand names are called terms and help developers to\nexpress specific identifiers in a compact manner. The @context keyword is described in detail in § 3.1 The Context.\n@direction\nUsed to set the base direction of a JSON-LD value, which are not typed values (e.g. strings, or language-tagged strings). This keyword is described in\n§ 4.2.4 String Internationalization.\n@graph\nUsed to express a graph. This keyword is described in § 4.9 Named Graphs.\n@id\nUsed to uniquely identify node objects that are being de",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
