      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Note",
      "pageStart": 13,
      "pageEnd": 15,
      "target": "../sections/sec-023-note.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Resolution of relative references to context URLs also applies to remote context documents, as they may themselves contain references to other\ncontexts.\nJSON documents can be interpreted as JSON-LD without having to be modified by referencing a context via an HTTP Link Header as described in\n§ 6.1 Interpreting JSON as JSON-LD. It is also possible to apply a custom context using the JSON-LD 1.1 API [JSON-LD11-API].\nIn JSON-LD documents, contexts may also be specified inline. This has the advantage that documents can be processed even in the absence of a\nconnection to the Web. Ultimately, this i",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
