      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Note",
      "pageStart": 19,
      "pageEnd": 19,
      "target": "../sections/sec-029-note.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "When possible, the context definition should be put at the top of a JSON-LD document. This makes the document easier to read and might make\nstreaming parsers more efficient. Documents that do not have the context at the top are still conformant JSON-LD.\nNote\nTo avoid forward-compatibility issues, terms starting with an @ character followed exclusively by one or more ALPHA characters (see [RFC5234])\nare to be avoided as they might be used as keyword in future versions of JSON-LD. Terms starting with an @ character that are not JSON-LD 1.1\nkeywords are treated as any other term, i.e., they are i",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
