      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Base IRI",
      "pageStart": 21,
      "pageEnd": 21,
      "target": "../sections/sec-033-413-base-iri.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "For example, if a JSON-LD document was retrieved from http://example.com/document.jsonld, relative IRI references would resolve against\nthat IRI:\nThis document uses an empty @id, which resolves to the document base. However, if the document is moved to a different location, the IRI would\nchange. To prevent this without having to use an IRI, a context may define an @base mapping, to overwrite the base IRI for the document.\nSetting @base to null will prevent relative IRI references from being expanded to IRIs.\nPlease note that the @base will be ignored if used in external contexts.\nThis section",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
