    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-034",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Using the Document Base for the Default Vocabulary",
      "pageStart": 21,
      "pageEnd": 22,
      "target": "../sections/sec-034-414-using-the-document-base-for-the-default-voca.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Example 29: Using \"#\" as the vocabulary mapping\n{\n  \"@context\": {\nIf this document were located at http://example/document, it would expand as follows:\nThis section is non-normative.\nA compact IRI is a way of expressing an IRI using a prefix and suffix separated by a colon (:). The prefix is a term taken from the active context and\nis a short string identifying a particular IRI in a JSON-LD document. For example, the prefix foaf may be used as a shorthand for the Friend-of-a-\nFriend vocabulary, which is identified using the IRI http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/. A developer may append any of the FOAF",
      "truncated": true,
