        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "IRI Expansion within a Context",
      "pageStart": 24,
      "pageEnd": 25,
      "target": "../sections/sec-038-417-iri-expansion-within-a-context.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Example 39: IRI expansion within a context\n{\n  \"@context\": {\n    \"xsd\": \"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#\",\n    \"name\": \"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name\",\n    \"age\": {\n      \"@id\": \"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/age\",\n⚠\nIn this example, the xsd term is defined and used as a prefix for the @type coercion of the age property.\nTerms may also be used when defining the IRI of another term:\nCompact IRIs and IRIs may be used on the left-hand side of a term definition.\nIn this example, the compact IRI form is used in two different ways. In the first approach, foaf:age declares both the IRI for the term (u",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
