      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-039",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Warning",
      "pageStart": 25,
      "pageEnd": 26,
      "target": "../sections/sec-039-warning.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "If a compact IRI is used as a term, it must expand to the value that compact IRI would have on its own when expanded. This represents a change\nto the original 1.0 algorithm to prevent terms from expanding to a different IRI, which could lead to undesired results.\n      \"@type\": \"xsd:integer\"\n    },\n    \"homepage\": {\n      \"@id\": \"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/homepage\",\n      \"@type\": \"@id\"\n    }\n  },\n  ...\n}\nExample 40: Using a term to define the IRI of another term within a context\n{\n  \"@context\": {\n    \"foaf\": \"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/\",\n    \"xsd\": \"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#\",\n    \"na",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
