      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Scoped Contexts",
      "pageStart": 26,
      "pageEnd": 27,
      "target": "../sections/sec-040-418-scoped-contexts.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Input\nExample 45: Defining an @context within a term definition\nCompacted (Input) \nExpanded (Result) \nStatements \nTurtle Open in playground\n{\n  \"@context\": {\n    \"@version\": 1.1,\n    \"name\": \"http://schema.org/name\",\n    \"interest\": {\n      \"@id\": \"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/interest\",\n      \"@context\": {\"@vocab\": \"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/\"}\n    }\n  },\n  \"name\": \"Manu Sporny\",\n  \"interest\": {\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.w3.org/TR/json-ld11/\",\n    \"name\": \"JSON-LD\",\nIn this case, the social profile is defined using the schema.org vocabulary, but interest is imported from FOAF, and is used to defin",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-041",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Note",
      "pageStart": 27,
      "pageEnd": 28,
      "target": "../sections/sec-041-note.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Any property-scoped or local contexts that were introduced in the node object would still be in effect when traversing into another node object.\nWhen expanding, each value of @type is considered (ordering them lexicographically) where that value is also a term in the active context having its\nown type-scoped context. If so, that the scoped context is applied to the active context.\nNote\nThe values of @type are unordered, so if multiple types are listed, the order that type-scoped contexts are applied is based on lexicographical\nordering.\nFor example, consider the following semantically equivale",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-042",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Note",
      "pageStart": 28,
      "pageEnd": 28,
      "target": "../sections/sec-042-note.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "If a term defines a scoped context, and then that term is later redefined, the association of the context defined in the earlier expanded term definition\nis lost within the scope of that redefinition. This is consistent with term definitions of a term overriding previous term definitions from earlier less\ndeeply nested definitions, as discussed in § 4.1 Advanced Context Usage.\nNote\nScoped Contexts are a new feature in JSON-LD 1.1.\nThis section is non-normative.\nOnce introduced, contexts remain in effect until a subsequent context removes it by setting @context to null, or by redefining terms,",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-043",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Context Propagation",
      "pageStart": 28,
      "pageEnd": 29,
      "target": "../sections/sec-043-419-context-propagation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Note\nContexts included within an array must all have the same value for @propagate due to the way that rollback is defined in JSON-LD 1.1 Processing\nAlgorithms and API.\nThis section is non-normative.\nJSON-LD 1.0 included mechanisms for modifying the context that is in effect. This included the capability to load and process a remote context and\nthen apply further changes to it via new contexts.\nHowever, with the introduction of JSON-LD 1.1, it is also desirable to be able to load a remote context, in particular an existing JSON-LD 1.0\ncontext, and apply JSON-LD 1.1 features to it prior to proc",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-044",
