      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Alternate Document Location",
      "pageStart": 69,
      "pageEnd": 69,
      "target": "../sections/sec-097-62-alternate-document-location.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Ordinary JSON documents can be interpreted as JSON-LD by providing an explicit JSON-LD context document. One way to provide this is by using\nreferencing a JSON-LD context document in an HTTP Link Header. Doing so allows JSON to be unambiguously machine-readable without requiring\ndevelopers to drastically change their documents and provides an upgrade path for existing infrastructure without breaking existing clients that rely\non the application/json media type or a media type with a +json suffix as defined in [RFC6839].\nIn order to use an external context with an ordinary JSON document, when r",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-098",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
