      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Modifying Behavior with Link Relationships",
      "pageStart": 69,
      "pageEnd": 70,
      "target": "../sections/sec-098-6-modifying-behavior-with-link-relationships.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "6.1 Interpreting JSON as JSON-LD §\nthe active context is initialized with the referenced external context. A response MUST NOT contain more than one HTTP Link Header using the\nhttp://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld#context link relation.\nOther mechanisms for providing a JSON-LD Context MAY be described for other URI schemes.\nThe JSON-LD 1.1 Processing Algorithms and API specification [JSON-LD11-API] provides for an expandContext option for specifying a context to\nuse when expanding JSON documents programmatically.\nThe following example demonstrates the use of an external context with an ordinary JSON do",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-099",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Note",
      "pageStart": 70,
      "pageEnd": 71,
      "target": "../sections/sec-099-note.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Example 142: Referencing a JSON-LD context from a JSON document via an HTTP Link Header\nGET /ordinary-json-document.json HTTP/1.1\nHost: example.com\nAccept: application/ld+json,application/json,*/*;q=0.1\n====================================\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\n...\nContent-Type: application/json\nLink: <https://json-ld.org/contexts/person.jsonld>; rel=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld#context\"; type=\"application/ld+json\"\n{\n  \"name\": \"Markus Lanthaler\",\n  \"homepage\": \"http://www.markus-lanthaler.com/\",\n  \"image\": \"http://twitter.com/account/profile_image/markuslanthaler\"\n}\n6.2 Alternate Document Location",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
