      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-100",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Note",
      "pageStart": 71,
      "pageEnd": 71,
      "target": "../sections/sec-100-note.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "This section describes features available with a documentLoader supporting HTML script extraction. See Remote Document and Context Retrieval\nfor more information.\nJSON-LD content can be easily embedded in HTML [HTML] by placing it in a script element with the type attribute set to application/ld+json.\nDoing so creates a data block.\nDefining how such data may be used is beyond the scope of this specification. The embedded JSON-LD document might be extracted as is or, e.g., be\ninterpreted as RDF.\nIf JSON-LD content is extracted as RDF [RDF11-CONCEPTS], it MUST be expanded into an RDF Dataset usi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-101",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Inheriting base IRI from HTML's base element",
      "pageStart": 71,
      "pageEnd": 72,
      "target": "../sections/sec-101-71-inheriting-base-iri-from-htmls-base-element.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Input\nExample 146: Using the document base URL to establish the default base IRI\nCompacted (Input) \nExpanded (Result) \nStatements \nTurtle\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <base href=\"http://dbpedia.org/resource/\"/>\n    <script type=\"application/ld+json\">\n    {\n      \"@context\": \"https://json-ld.org/contexts/person.jsonld\",\n      \"@id\": \"John_Lennon\",\n      \"name\": \"John Lennon\",\n      \"born\": \"1940-10-09\",\n      \"spouse\": \"Cynthia_Lennon\"\nHTML allows for Dynamic changes to base URLs. This specification does not require any specific behavior, and to ensure that all systems process\nthe base IRI equivalently,",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-102",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Note",
      "pageStart": 72,
      "pageEnd": 72,
      "target": "../sections/sec-102-note.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Such content should be escaped as indicated below, however the content will remain escaped after processing through the JSON-LD API [JSON-\nLD11-API].\n&amp; → & (ampersand, U+0026)\n&lt; → < (less-than sign, U+003C)\n&gt; → > (greater-than sign, U+003E)\n&quot; → \" (quotation mark, U+0022)\n&apos; → ' (apostrophe, U+0027)\nA specific script element within an HTML document may be located using a fragment identifier matching the unique identifier of the script element\nwithin the HTML document located by a URL (see [DOM]). A JSON-LD processor MUST extract only the specified data block's contents parsin",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
