    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-105",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Data Model",
      "pageStart": 73,
      "pageEnd": 73,
      "target": "../sections/sec-105-8-data-model.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "To ease understanding for developers unfamiliar with the RDF model, the following summary is provided:\nA JSON-LD document serializes a RDF Dataset [RDF11-CONCEPTS], which is a collection of graphs that comprises exactly one default\ngraph and zero or more named graphs.\nThe default graph does not have a name and MAY be empty.\nEach named graph is a pair consisting of an IRI or blank node identifier (the graph name) and a graph. Whenever practical, the graph name\nSHOULD be an IRI.\nA graph is a labeled directed graph, i.e., a set of nodes connected by directed-arcs.\nEvery directed-arc is labeled wi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-106",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Note",
      "pageStart": 73,
      "pageEnd": 74,
      "target": "../sections/sec-106-note.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The use of blank node identifiers to label properties is obsolete, and may be removed in a future version of JSON-LD. Consider using a\ndocument-relative IRI, instead, such as #.\nEvery node is an IRI, a blank node, or a literal, although syntactically lists and native JSON values may be represented directly.\nA node having an outgoing edge MUST be an IRI or a blank node.\nA graph MUST NOT contain unconnected nodes, i.e., nodes which are not connected by an property to any other node.\nNote\nThis effectively just prohibits unnested, empty node objects and unnested node objects that contain only an @",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-107",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Note",
      "pageStart": 74,
      "pageEnd": 75,
      "target": "../sections/sec-107-note.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Input\nExample 150: Linked Data Dataset\nCompacted (Input) \nExpanded (Result) \nStatements \nTriG\n{\n  \"@context\": [\n    \"http://schema.org/\",\n    {\"@base\": \"http://example.com/\"}\n  ],\n  \"@graph\": [{\n    \"@id\": \"people/alice\",\n    \"gender\": [\n      {\"@value\": \"weiblich\", \"@language\": \"de\"},\n      {\"@value\": \"female\",   \"@language\": \"en\"}\n    ],\n    \"knows\": {\"@id\": \"people/bob\"},\n    \"name\": \"Alice\"\n  }, {\n    \"@id\": \"graphs/1\",\n    \"@graph\": {\n      \"@id\": \"people/alice\",\n      \"parent\": {\n        \"@id\": \"people/bob\",\n        \"name\": \"Bob\"\n      }\n    }\n  }, {\n    \"@id\": \"graphs/2\",\n    \"@graph\":",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-108",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Terms",
      "pageStart": 75,
      "pageEnd": 75,
      "target": "../sections/sec-108-91-terms.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "A node object represents zero or more properties of a node in the graph serialized by the JSON-LD document. A map is a node object if it exists\noutside of a JSON-LD context and:\nit is not the top-most map in the JSON-LD document consisting of no other entries than @graph and @context,\nit does not contain the @value, @list, or @set keywords, and\nit is not a graph object.\nThe properties of a node in a graph may be spread among different node objects within a document. When that happens, the keys of the different node\nobjects need to be merged to create the properties of the resulting node.\nA nod",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-109",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Node Objects",
      "pageStart": 75,
      "pageEnd": 75,
      "target": "../sections/sec-109-92-node-objects.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "empty"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-110",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "JSON-LD Grammar",
      "pageStart": 75,
      "pageEnd": 76,
      "target": "../sections/sec-110-9-json-ld-grammar.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "9.1 Terms §\n9.2 Node Objects §\nIf the node object contains the @type key, its value MUST be either an IRI reference, a compact IRI (including blank node identifiers), a term defined\nin the active context expanding into an IRI, or an array of any of these. See § 3.5 Specifying the Type for further discussion on @type values.\nIf the node object contains the @reverse key, its value MUST be a map containing entries representing reverse properties. Each value of such a\nreverse property MUST be an IRI reference, a compact IRI, a blank node identifier, a node object or an array containing a combinati",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-111",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Frame Objects",
      "pageStart": 76,
      "pageEnd": 76,
      "target": "../sections/sec-111-93-frame-objects.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "A graph object represents a named graph, which MAY include an explicit graph name. A map is a graph object if it exists outside of a JSON-LD\ncontext, it contains an @graph entry (or an alias of that keyword), it is not the top-most map in the JSON-LD document, and it consists of no entries\nother than @graph, @index, @id and @context, or an alias of one of these keywords.\nIf the graph object contains the @context key, its value MUST be null, an IRI reference, a context definition, or an array composed of any of these.\nIf the graph object contains the @id key, its value is used as the identifier",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-112",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Graph Objects",
      "pageStart": 76,
      "pageEnd": 76,
      "target": "../sections/sec-112-94-graph-objects.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "empty"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/w3c-2020-json-ld-1-1/blocks/prose-sec-113",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Value Objects",
      "pageStart": 76,
      "pageEnd": 77,
      "target": "../sections/sec-113-95-value-objects.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "A value object MUST be a map containing the @value key. It MAY also contain an @type, an @language, an @direction, an @index, or an @context\nkey but MUST NOT contain both an @type and either @language or @direction keys at the same time. A value object MUST NOT contain any other\nkeys that expand to an IRI or keyword.\nThe value associated with the @value key MUST be either a string, a number, true, false or null. If the value associated with the @type key is\n@json, the value MAY be either an array or an object.\nThe value associated with the @type key MUST be a term, an IRI, a compact IRI, a str",
